 ${misc:Depends},
Suggests: tpm2-tools, swtpm
Description: verify TPM 2.0 endorsement key certificates and their vendor chain
 tpm2-verifier reads the endorsement key (EK) certificates and the vendor
 certificate chain from a TPM 2.0 (Linux /dev/tpmrm0, Windows TBS or swtpm)
 and verifies them up to a curated, fingerprint-pinned store of TPM vendor
 root CAs, including CRL revocation checks and AIA chain completion.
 .
 With -prove it also shows that the TPM holds the private key of each EK
 certificate, by recreating the EK from its TCG template and decrypting a
 challenge with TPM2_ActivateCredential.
 .
 Debug bundles and anonymized vendor information help adding TPM vendors that
 are not in the store yet.
